  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1231 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nOur extended period of dangerous heat is going to continue through\nat least Friday. Highs Thursday will once again be in the mid to\nupper 90s with some areas possibly seeing 100+ and heat index\nvalues as hot as 112. The upper level ridge will be closed off\nsitting to our east. Some weak upper level short waves will spin\naround this and kick off a low to medium chance for scattered \nthunderstorm activity. The chances will be mainly in the afternoon\nand evenings Thursday through Saturday. With the ridge flattening\nout some we will see gradual cooling Friday and Saturday but it\nwill still remain hot with highs in the mid to upper 90s and heat\nindex values as hot as 109. Low to medium thunderstorm chances\nwill remain in the forecast Sunday into next week as a trough digs\ninto the Great Lakes. The good new with this is it will cool us\nback closer to seasonal norms. Widespread organized storms are \nnot expected as we will have little to no wind shear but we will \nsee a ton of CAPE in the afternoon and evenings. This will bring a\nlow wind risk with any taller storms as they collapse. Brief \nheavy downpours can also be expected with any thunderstorms.",
